<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/software/polkit/policyconfig-1.dtd">

<!-- Lets the switch in the app do what "sudo modemctl" does from a terminal.

     allow_active is "yes", so the person at the phone is not asked for a
     password. That is a decision, not an oversight, and it rests on two
     things.

     The first is that there is nobody to ask. Phosh registers no polkit
     authentication agent, so an action set to auth_admin has no way to put a
     prompt on the screen: pkexec would simply fail, and the switch would be a
     button that does nothing. The audio switcher in the sibling project used
     to carry its own agent for exactly this reason, and was glad to be rid of
     it once audioctl no longer needed root. modemctl cannot follow it - it
     patches files under /usr/lib and writes /etc - so the choice is between
     this and no switch.

     The second is that it grants nothing that is not already granted.
     ofono2mm ships a bus policy handing group "radio" - which on this phone is
     the one human account - the whole ModemManager1.Modem interface, raw AT
     commands included, with no polkit check anywhere. A switch between the
     shipped state and the repaired one is a smaller capability than that by a
     wide margin.

     What keeps it from being a general-purpose root tool is in modemctl
     itself: as root it refuses every MODEMCTL_* override outright, so this
     cannot be pointed at an arbitrary file. That guard was written for the
     "sudo modemctl" case and covers this one unchanged.

     Not allow_any and not allow_inactive: a remote session or a switched-away
     seat has no business changing what the modem is doing. -->
<policyconfig>
  <vendor>misc-de</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/misc-de/furios_modem_fixes</vendor_url>

  <action id="de.misc-de.modemctl.switch">
    <description>Switch the modem between the shipped state and the repairs</description>
    <description xml:lang="de">Modem zwischen Auslieferungszustand und Reparaturen umschalten</description>
    <message>Changing the modem configuration</message>
    <message xml:lang="de">Die Modem-Konfiguration wird geändert</message>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>no</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>no</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>yes</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/bin/modemctl</annotate>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.allow_gui">true</annotate>
  </action>
</policyconfig>
